    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a867e099d420055fd99470634140dc1a40748d0cceb8ae7347442e98b6c71b24",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Gram signs provide inexpensive local lower-count evidence and package failures into Gram blocks, while Turing's construction converts corrected sign samples, parity of S at good Gram points, and an averaged S bound into an all-strip upper count. The reported finite verification follows only when the critical-line lower count and this independently derived total-count bound meet at the same integer.",
