    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fb472259dc516c1120d9dbc9f4dcdda3bf690ae3f62f024da292ce47d29b6c8e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The remainder approximation is built as a staged change of representation: the cutoff is aligned with a saddle, the contour is localized, dominant exponential and quadratic behavior is factored away, the residual power series is truncated and made termwise integrable, and grading plus recurrences compute only the coefficient combinations visible at the retained asymptotic orders. The later error discussion separates the principal analytic losses from finite-precision phase and summation error.",
